RynoX

An advanced, multipurpose Discord bot built with Python.

RynoX is a feature-rich Discord bot designed to help communities manage, protect, and customize their servers. It includes moderation tools, automoderation, antinuke protection, ticket management, logging, utility commands, games, and more.

Features

Moderation

- Ban and unban members
- Kick members
- Warnings management
- Timeout management
- Message purge
- Moderation utilities

Security & Protection

- Advanced antinuke system
- Honeypot protection
- Automoderation
- Webhook logging
- Server protection tools

Server Management

- Welcome and farewell system
- Autorole system
- Reaction roles
- Custom autoresponder
- Ticket system
- Server logging
- Giveaway management

Utility & Information

- User information
- Server information
- Channel information
- Role information
- Bot statistics
- Custom help menu

Fun & Games

- Tic-Tac-Toe
- Chess
- Wordle
- Connect Four
- Rock Paper Scissors
- 2048
- Country Guess
- Type Racer

Technology

- Python
- discord.py
- AsyncIO
- SQLite support
- JSON-based configuration
- Discord Slash Commands
- Modular Cog Architecture

Installation

1. Clone the repository

git clone YOUR_REPOSITORY_URL
cd RynoX-Bot

2. Install dependencies

pip install -r requirements.txt

3. Configure environment variables

Create a ".env" file in the project directory.

DISCORD_TOKEN=YOUR_BOT_TOKEN
BOT_PREFIX=.
CLIENT_ID=YOUR_CLIENT_ID
OWNER_IDS=YOUR_DISCORD_ID

WEBSITE=
SUPPORT_SERVER=
STATUS_PAGE=
INVITE_URL=

4. Start the bot

python main.py

Configuration

Variable| Description
"DISCORD_TOKEN"| Discord bot token
"BOT_PREFIX"| Default command prefix
"CLIENT_ID"| Discord application ID
"OWNER_IDS"| Bot owner IDs
"SUPPORT_SERVER"| Support server URL
"WEBSITE"| Website URL
"STATUS_PAGE"| Status page URL
"INVITE_URL"| Bot invitation URL

Additional webhook variables can be configured in ".env".

